From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:05:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] phy: samsung: add the gs201 MIPI DC-PHY receiver

The gs201 CSIS camera receiver links each sit behind a slave of the
Samsung MIPI DC-PHY: links 0 and 1 with four data lanes, links 2-7 with
two. An even two-lane slave and the odd one after it combine into one
four-lane receiver for the even link (the odd slave's two data lanes
come first in its window and its clock lane is unused). A bias block and
one PMU isolation bit are shared. Mainline only has the transmit
(master) side of this PHY family, in phy-rockchip-samsung-dcphy.

Add a generic PHY driver for the receive side. Power-on releases the
PMU isolation and the slave's reset bit in the CSIS sysreg (the lane
registers must not be touched while it is held), resets the analog part
with the lanes off, and programs the bias block, the clock lane and
each data lane. The register layout and sequence follow Google's GPL
phy-exynos-mipi.c for DC-PHY version 0x0504 and what the stock camera
software writes on Pixel 7 phones.

D-PHY and C-PHY are both supported. Google's GPL driver leaves C-PHY
unimplemented; a consumer selects it with
phy_set_mode_ext(PHY_MODE_MIPI_DPHY, PHY_TYPE_CPHY), and
phy_configure()'s lanes are then trios, one data lane block each, with
no clock lane and no four-lane pairing, and hs_clk_rate is the symbol
rate.

The receive settings themselves (the bias and per-lane analog words,
and the settle count and skew delay by rate) differ from Google's GPL
values and are not public, so they are not in this driver: it loads
them from a data file named by firmware-name at the first power-on, in
a small format of its own (an ordered list of writes per block and a
table by rate). The file is checked whole before anything is written,
and without it no link powers on. Lane registers can be dumped through
debugfs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/phy/samsung/Kconfig                   |  11 +
 drivers/phy/samsung/Makefile                  |   1 +
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-gs201-mipi-dcphy-rx.c | 856 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 868 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-gs201-mipi-dcphy-rx.c

diff --git a/drivers/phy/samsung/Kconfig b/drivers/phy/samsung/Kconfig
index b7ab40290..6849ced7a 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/samsung/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/phy/samsung/Kconfig
@@ -29,6 +29,17 @@ config PHY_EXYNOS_PCIE
 	  Enable PCIe PHY support for Exynos SoC series.
 	  This driver provides PHY interface for Exynos PCIe controller.
 
+config PHY_GS201_MIPI_DCPHY
+	tristate "Google gs201 MIPI DC-PHY receiver driver"
+	depends on OF && (ARCH_EXYNOS || COMPILE_TEST)
+	depends on EXYNOS_PMU || COMPILE_TEST
+	select GENERIC_PHY
+	select GENERIC_PHY_MIPI_DPHY
+	help
+	  Enable support for the receive side of the MIPI DC-PHY of the
+	  Google gs201 (Tensor G2) SoC, used by its CSIS camera receiver.
+	  D-PHY only.
+
 config PHY_SAMSUNG_UFS
 	tristate "Exynos SoC series UFS PHY driver"
 	depends on OF && (ARCH_EXYNOS || COMPILE_TEST)
